# ACC02 + ACC03 + ACC04 acceptance, one gesture list:
#
#   B_DESKMENU  the *Desk* drop-down carries BOTH registered accessory titles
#               (one loaded from C:\ACC\, one from the root)
#   C_ALERT     picking the first one posts AC_OPEN to its owner, which runs
#               beside the parked desktop and shows its form_alert
#   D_DISMISSED the alert's OK is the accessory's own click; the desktop
#               screen comes back untouched
#   E_ALERT2    the SECOND accessory answers its own menu entry -- the two
#               are distinct processes with distinct menu ids
#   F_BACK      dismissed again
#   G_WINDOW    the desktop is still usable beside them: DISK C opens its
#               window (the point of ACC03)
#   H_GEMWIN    a GEM program launched from that window runs (it lives 6 s
#               by its own `evnt_timer`, so the mark sits inside that window);
#               its start went
#               through the desktop's appl_exit, which posted AC_CLOSE to both
#               accessories and blocked until both had seen it (serial)
#   I_AFTER     the program terminated by itself and the desktop is back
#
# Coordinates from the probe run (method/probe.actions): *Desk* title (20,9);
# Desk box entries (104,59) and (104,75); the alert's OK button (319,277) from
# acc1-alert.png; DISK C (38,35); GEMWIN.NAP in the C:\ window (179,187).
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 20 9
2400 mark B_DESKMENU
3000 move 104 59
3400 down
3403 up
3600 move 600 300
4600 mark C_ALERT
5200 move 319 277
5600 down
5603 up
5800 move 600 300
6800 mark D_DISMISSED
7400 move 20 9
8200 move 104 75
8600 down
8603 up
8800 move 600 300
9800 mark E_ALERT2
10400 move 319 277
10800 down
10803 up
11000 move 600 300
12000 mark F_BACK
12600 move 37 42
12800 down
12803 up
12810 down
12813 up
13400 move 600 300
14400 mark G_WINDOW
15000 move 179 187
15200 down
